{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/63616-forms-of-magic-other-then-sorcery-and-necromancy","id":63616,"title":"Forms of Magic other then Sorcery and Necromancy","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-02T15:30:50-08:00","id":63616,"title":"Forms of Magic other then Sorcery and Necromancy","content":"So just like that.<br /> <br /> 1) Considering that there are already two distinct systems of magic at the very least, why couldn't there be more?<br /> *well, also there is Grace Magic, but it is very different and charismatic thing in and of itself*<br /> <br /> <br /> 2) What would be the consequences of taking up those studies of essence manipulation? Same as with canonical ones - directly cutting off ways to develop other magics, following common trope of &quot;not been able to learn incompatible martial arts&quot;; or probably hindering subsequent progress of magic practice - adding additional XP cost of learning new spells based on the number of Magic Systems unlocked by user; or something else completely - not even troubling perhaps?<br /> <br /> <br /> 3) Also, all spoilers on new edition's sorcery with gathering external world essence just cry to me of &quot;Onepower&quot; from &quot;Wheel of Time&quot; and Warhammer's &quot;Winds of magic&quot;. So I won't be surprised at all to see some kind of variation of Angreals and Sa'angreals - I probably would be amazed to not see any. And it drives me to this thought: &quot;what kind of thing should describe character's aptitude and mastery of manipulating essence for such ends?&quot; Cause, I don't think that Occult ability covers it like that and other obvious alternative - Essence trait - defines inner workings of being and its potential. Maybe there is a need for some specific synthetic skill of &quot;essence manipulation&quot; unlocking only after getting access to Sorcery and working with such magics only? Or some other way?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And as I am the one to start this topic, I should present a few takes on it of my own.<br /> <br /> <i><i>Elemental Mastery</i></i><br /> <br /> Yeah, just like in Avatar or FMA - extend your essence outside and take a hold of physical elements of Creation. I can totally see Dragon-Bloods developing this kind of discipline in response to Solars discovering Sorcery or after ending of the Usurpation, when it was their golden time. Perhaps there might be at least two Circles for this practice - first giving access to main five elements; second allowing manipulation of derivative and composed elements, like metal, glass, ice, etc; and third... should be something like that all BIG and luminous Avatar-mode or operation of elements on abstract level as metaphors? System should be based around &quot;Element initiation&quot; charms, representing access to particular elements and spells working as distinct ways to manipulate them, probably.<br /> <br /> <i>Runic magic</i><br /> <br /> Well, you know, those fancy concepts of letters and words being so full of senses and meanings that they weight too heavy on the world and warp the reality itself. Seems pretty well aligned with Exalted stuff.<br /> <br /> <i>Battle Magic</i><br /> <br /> Not just aggressive spells for fight, but form of simplified essence weaving with limited number of effects solely for combat use, like shielding, damaging, suppressing, etc. In compensation it should be truly fast. Something along the lines of Kido from Bleach. It seems pretty reasonable for mortal essence users from current exalted editions.<br /> <br /> <i>Wyld magic</i><br /> <br /> Yeah, I think there must be magic of operation chaos energies from &quot;Creation perspective&quot;, not just some charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2156-overbound","name":"Overbound","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-02T15:46:17-08:00","id":63623,"title":"","content":"That is kind of what I'm hoping this (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/59488-sorcery-3e-spoiler-hey-look-vance-can-provide-non-napkin-spoilers-sometimes\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...lers-sometimes</a>) is about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-02T19:57:15-08:00","id":63704,"title":"","content":"The problem with this, as I see it, is how you make it all thematically distinct. I mean, Sorcery is vague enough as it is.<br /> <br /> Avatar-style bending? Use only elemental spells, follow the Salinan school of philosophy - most spells are created by studying and embracing nature.<br /> <br /> Runic Magic? Also completely possible - that's what Silurian Symbology is all about; deciphering the graphic representations of the concepts that make up reality, thus enabling (relatively) quick and easy substitution leading to things like Death of Golden Butterflies or Lightning Kraken.<br /> <br /> Battle Magic... Sounds a lot more like a esoteric-yet-straightforward Martial Art to me. Quick Summary; Sorcery (AKA &quot;True Magic&quot;) is direct reshaping of Reality to your will, using Transcendent understanding of the nature of Reality and Self. It was given to the Exalted by the Yozis, in one of their first plans to escape - it should come as no surprise that the Ebon Dragon was behind it. Supernatural Martial Arts, on the other hand, involves mastering your essence, training with it until you can use it in unnatural ways. It grew out of mundane martial arts, the Exalted practitioners realising that they could control, train and master their Animas as well as their bodies.<br /> <br /> Wyld Magic? That's... Pretty much what Sorcery is. There's literally no reason why you couldn't make a spell that would let you pull off &quot;Wyld-Shaping&quot; inside Creation proper - the tricky bit is to set the scope and cost to reasonable levels, so as to not be too blatant a rip-off of the Solar Charm. Which I still maintain should have been a spell in the first place.<br /> <br /> You even missed one; Devonian Sorcery is all about SCIENCE! It's behind all the nifty magitech they had in the First Age, such as essence cannons, skyships, power armour and cache eggs... Which are really just one stunt and a mind control charm away from being pokeballs. Think of the possibilities!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Aretii: &quot;As one of the players described it, 'After initiation, it was actually a relief seeing who had eyepatches or bandaged hands - you know what <i>they</i> sacrificed, instead of wondering what bits people cut out of their own souls to gain power.'&quot;","edited":{"userid":578,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/578-lord-sia","user":"Lord Sia","date":". 02-17-2014, 01:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/578-lord-sia","name":"Lord Sia","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-02T20:39:47-08:00","id":63729,"title":"","content":"<a 