rd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T00:07:27-08:00","id":63801,"title":"","content":"That video feels like a Raksha to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T00:36:23-08:00","id":63811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/63616-forms-of-magic-other-then-sorcery-and-necromancy?p=63729#post63729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://vimeo.com/44126386\" target=\"_blank\">SEIZON SENRYAKU!</a></div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Listen up, you low-lifes who will never amount to anything.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/726-amine-hsu","name":"Amine Hsu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar726_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T01:31:42-08:00","id":63823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/63616-forms-of-magic-other-then-sorcery-and-necromancy?p=63778#post63778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still! Thank you. Glad to have the series named and a supposition of the scene's contextual meaning from someone with better knowledge of the show than me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't get me wrong, this was with about two minutes of discussion with a friend who has actually seen it (I have not), and me answering a handful of his questions about Exalted. As guesses go, it's... not very useful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Once, there was a maiden... who spent all her time on the internet.<br /> &quot;Someone out there is WRONG,&quot; she said.<br /> So she tossed a noose made of golden light... and strangled her opponent.<br /> Both of them died alone.<br /> &quot;Love is for football players and cheerleaders,&quot; her obituary said.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/261-notthepenguins","name":"notthepenguins","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar261_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"359"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T03:27:06-08:00","id":63855,"title":"","content":"In another thread, TDO* was involved in a short discussion about Magical Girl Transformation (or a &quot;Pulp Sorceress&quot; equivalent for a not-particularly-silly Exalted game) as a paradigm for the use of sorcery, and commented about how he figured out how to implement it in EX3. He also said it was not something likely to show up in the Core Book, but that he was holding onto the idea.<br /> <br /> I'm also pretty sure he referred to it as Magical Girl Transformation/Seizon Senryaku, linking to the same clip as he linked above.<br /> <br /> <b>EDIT</b>: Also, this fantastic quote:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/30720-sorcery-tdo-spoilers-and-you-thought-the-ma-napkins-were-bad-huh?p=33673#post33673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mawaru Penguindrum is a show that reels you in with the bait of &quot;haha what the fuck this is so weird&quot; to set you up for a soul-breaking sucker punch to the genitalia of your heart. I highly recommend it!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> *<span style=\"font-size:10px\">I should probably stop with that. Especially once EX3 is finally here, calling him that will be quite confusing for the newly arrived fans, now that he goes by his actual name...</span><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":868,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","user":"danelsan","date":". 02-03-2014, 06:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T04:03:45-08:00","id":63866,"title":"","content":".......It's not really a Magical Girl Transformation sequence. I mean it sorta is but not really. It's complicated.<br /> It's a very strange series where the 'Child Boiler' is a real non-allegorical thing. I'm not even really sure how to explain it without tossing out spoilers all over the place but I think I kinda know what he might be referring to...<br /> <br /> <br /> (( also, my previous comment was a quite from the character in the video so it wasn't completely random ))","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/726-amine-hsu","name":"Amine Hsu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar726_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T05:36:30-08:00","id":63895,"title":"","content":"Ahh, Mawaru Penguindrum. I think it beats Revolutionary Girl Utena in being Ikuhara's strangest series.And yet, despite how silly it was, it really explored some pretty mature themes about life, death and second chances (or not as the case may be).<br /> <br /> Without spoiling too much, the previous guess regarding Liminals is probably the closest since saving the ones that you love from death is a central plot point throughout the series. According to the Liminal Preview, the sorcerer is very desperate to the point that it describes him drawing power from multiple sources in his vast ritual. Only the Entity in the Underworld actually does anything.The description may suggest that there are multiple avenues of power but anything beyond that is mostly conjecture.<br /> <br /> To the question of other forms of magic. I feel that the paths and initiations you take in order to obtain the power to influence essence directly is more important than the end result.<br /> <br /> Sorry for my limited English. I'll go back to being just an observer now.<br /> <br /> Edit: Vance's Link doesn't work anymore, so here is a new one. <a href=\"https://www.nicovideo.jp/watch/sm14972985\" target=\"_blank\"> Seizon Senryaku </a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>How can I know if what I claim I know to be true is rejecting the idea that there is something I might not know? How can I know if what I claim I don't know to be true is rejecting the idea that there is something I do know?<br /> -Zhuangzi","edited":{"userid":1715,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1715-ostarion","user":"Ostarion","date":". 04-12-2019, 05:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1715-ostarion","name":"Ostarion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1715_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"305"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T09:00:48-08:00","id":69865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/63616-forms-of-magic-other-then-sorcery-and-necromancy?p=63623#post63623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is kind of what I'm hoping this (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/59488-sorcery-3e-spoiler-hey-look-vance-can-provide-non-napkin-spoilers-sometimes\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...lers-sometimes</a>) is about.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm. When I read that statement, I interpreted it pretty much as \u201cthere are different ways to get Enlightened essence with minor flavor differences\u201d just with implication to the Sorcery.<br /> But after giving it a second thought I might get the idea of what you are putting in that.<br /> Something along the line, that every mage could possibly cast \u201cEssence blast\u201d spell, but\u2026<br /> * casting it through the lens of \u201cShadow Initiation\u201d u\u2019ll get \u201cDark arrow\u201d, which is a lot easier to gather essence for during the night and that much harder under the Sun\u2019s reign;<br /> * casting the same spell with \u201cStygian Initiation\u201d performs \u201cEntropic blast\u201d, which is truly destructive to the shadows of dead, but not so much for those still alive as their own live essence protects them;<br /> * and \u201cSolar Initiation\u201d will produce some kind of \u201cLight spear\u201d which power doesn\u2019t depend on some inconsistent changeable factors of the world and lights everywhere with the same power;<br /> * oh, and through the \u201cWyld Initiation\u201d it\u2019s totally possible to send a freaking rainbow up ur enemy\u2019s ass, with every subsequent spell being easier to cast as chaos energies temporarily blur strict frames of Creation\u2019s essence movement.<br /> <br /> Under this point of view it doesn\u2019t seem too bad to me. Pretty damn good, I should probably say. And with each form of initiation having its own trademark spells (u certainly can raise zombies with \u201cSolar Initiation\u201d buy filling them with the life they\u2019ve lost, but it\u2019s SO MUCH easier to do it through the \u201cUnlife energies\u201d, and same goes for the mind controlling spells).<br /> Hm\u2026<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Sia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/63616-forms-of-magic-other-then-sorcery-and-necromancy?p=63704#post63704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with this, as I see it, is how you make it all thematically distinct. I mean, Sorcery is vague enough as it is.<br /> <br /> Avatar-style bending? Use only elemental spells, follow the Salinan school of philosophy - most spells are created by studying and embracing nature.<br /> <br /> Runic Magic? Also completely possible - that's what Silurian Symbology is all about; deciphering the graphic representations of the concepts that make up reality, thus enabling (relatively) quick and easy substitution leading to things like Death of Golden Butterflies or Lightning Kraken.<br /> <br /> Battle Magic... Sounds a lot more like a esoteric-yet-straightforward Martial Art to me. Quick Summary; Sorcery (AKA &quot;True Magic&quot;) is direct reshaping of Reality to your will, using Transcendent understanding of the nature of Reality and Self. It was given to the Exalted by the Yozis, in one of their first (totally botched) plans to escape - it should come as no surprise that the Ebon Dragon was behind it. Supernatural Martial Arts, on the other hand, involves mastering your essence, training with it until you can use it in unnatural ways. It grew out of mundane martial arts, the Exalted practitioners realising that they could control, train and mastery their Animas as well as their bodies.<br /> <br /> Wyld Magic? That's... Pretty much what Sorcery is. There's literally no reason why you couldn't make a spell that would let you pull off &quot;Wyld-Shaping&quot; inside Creation proper - the tricky bit is to set the scope and cost to reasonable levels, so as to not be too blatant a rip-off of the Solar Charm. Which I still maintain should have been a spell in the first place.<br /> <br /> You even missed one; Devonian Sorcery is all about SCIENCE! It's behind all the nifty magitech they had in the First Age, such as essence cannons, skyships, power armour and cache eggs... Which are really just one stunt and a mind control charm away from being pokeballs. Think of the possibilities!</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, didn\u2019t know about those exalted sorcery schools, but I can see where u\u2019re coming from. But that\u2019s a point to be made only if Sorcery is a single system with different interpretations of using it and it contradicts having Necromancy as its\u2019 own thing \u2013 not just thematic subset of Sorcery. Else it should be at least possible to make them as powerful in their own central ideas as Sorcery (and I mean not just by adding more POWAR!!! but through the unique qualities of their\u2019s).<br /> <br /> Heck, those were just some random examples of my own understanding of the topic to get some feedback. Just thinking of classic Elven races inspires to at least two more forms of magic \u2013 one operating through the themes of (Immortality/Mortality/ Endless/Endings/Continuations) and another through the inner nature of things.<br /> <br /> P.S. Sorry for all possible mistakes and bad idea transaction \u2013 English isn\u2019t my native language and writing ain\u2019t the same as reading))<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2156-overbound","name":"Overbound","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-17T10:27:38-08:00","id":73784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus878</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/63616-forms-of-magic-other-then-sorcery-and-necromancy?p=63745#post63745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">MissMaddy, how could you forget about the <b>VANCIAN</b> magic system? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'd actually do that as thaumaturgy - you spend an hour performing a ritual, which you can then complete at any time using a miscellaneous action. Extra successes on the ritual roll reduces the time, and assorted Charms - including a couple of &quot;Schools of Magic&quot; Terrestrial Martial Arts - enhances it further, reducing the time, allowing you to prepare and/or cast multiple instances of the same spell, replace costly ingredients and tools with motes and then reduces the price of doing so, etc. Performing rituals with a power akin to that of true Sorcery would be the capstone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Aretii: &quot;As one of the players described it, 'After initiation, it was actually a relief seeing who had eyepatches or bandaged hands - you know what <i>they</i> sacrificed, instead of wondering what bits people cut out of their own souls to gain power.'&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/578-lord-sia","name":"Lord Sia","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-17T11:16:09-08:00","id":73800,"title":"","content":"I always liked the thought of practical alchemy.<br /> <br /> In fact, when I first heard of Alchemicals, I thought that's what they were: mortals that perfected their bodies and exalted through alchemy. I was very confused as to why they were communist robots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/845-dragonmystic","name":"Dragonmystic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar845_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-17T11:55:52-08:00","id":73817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ostarion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/63616-forms-of-magic-other-then-sorcery-and-necromancy?p=63895#post63895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ahh, Mawaru Penguindrum. I think it beats Revolutionary Girl Utena in being Ikuhara's strangest series.And yet, despite how silly it was, it really explored some pretty mature themes about life, death and second chances (or not as the case may be).<br /> <br /> Without spoiling too much, the previous guess regarding Liminals is probably the closest since saving the ones that you love from death is a central plot point throughout the series. According to the Liminal Preview, the sorcerer is very desperate to the point that it describes him drawing power from multiple sources in his vast ritual. Only the Entity in the Underworld actually does anything.The description may suggest that there are multiple avenues of power but anything beyond that is mostly conjecture.<br /> <br /> To the question of other forms of magic. I feel that the paths and initiations you take in order to obtain the power to influence essence directly is more important than the end result.<br /> <br /> Sorry for my limited English. I'll go back to being just an observer now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Himari wouldn't make a very good Liminal Character. She's much better represented in Chuubo's Marvelous Wish-Granting Engine as a Creature of the Light.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-17T14:14:29-08:00","id":73876,"title":"","content":"Hmm, let me think about it for a while. Himari does not seem to fit the classification of Liminal, but I don't know enough about Creatures of Light to agree so I need to do some research and maybe re-watch some episodes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>How can I know if what I claim I know to be true is rejecting the idea that there is something I might not know? How can I know if what I claim I don't know to be true is rejecting the idea that there is something I do know?<br /> -Zhuangzi","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1715-ostarion","name":"Ostarion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1715_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"305"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-12T02:47:51-07:00","id":1304420,"title":"","content":"Well, In case anyone likes using Ikuhara's stuff for the strange magics and mutations that you can steal, he released a new series called Sarazanmai, which is surprisingly a majority male cast (biologically it should be noted, let's not forget how different gender can be in his works).<br /> <br /> I can already imagine some strange being able to steal mythical organs from your body (perhaps not like the Shirikodama which is a bit much). Anyway check it out on crunchyroll.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/63616-forms-of-magic-other-then-sorcery-and-necromancy?p=73817#post73817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Himari wouldn't make a very good Liminal Character. She's much better represented in Chuubo's Marvelous Wish-Granting Engine as a Creature of the Light.</div> </div> </div> </div>After thinking about this for 5 years, and seeing actual descriptions and checking my post history to realize I didn't actually respond to this.............. I agree.<br /> <br /> So, what were you referring to with that reference?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>How can I know if what I claim I know to be true is rejecting the idea that there is something I might not know? How can I know if what I claim I don't know to be true is rejecting the idea that there is something I do know?<br /> -Zhuangzi","edited":{"userid":1715,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1715-ostarion","user":"Ostarion","date":". 04-12-2019, 05:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1715-ostarion","name":"Ostarion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1715_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"305"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-12T03:01:12-07:00","id":1304422,"title":"","content":"After five years does he even remember the reference?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-12T05:59:10-07:00","id":1304434,"title":"","content":"And lest we all forget BLESSED MAN-MACHINE WEAVING PROTOCOLS, THE GIFTS OF AUTOCHTHON.<br /> <br /> Also wow this thread came back from nowhere","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-12T08:16:38-07:00","id":1304442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ostarion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/63616-forms-of-magic-other-then-sorcery-and-necromancy?p=1304420#post1304420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, In case anyone likes using Ikuhara's stuff for the strange magics and mutations that you can steal, he released a new series called Sarazanmai, which is surprisingly a majority male cast (biologically it should be noted, let's not forget how different gender can be in his works).<br /> <br /> I can already imagine some strange being able to steal mythical organs from your body (perhaps not like the Shirikodama which is a bit much). Anyway check it out on crunchyroll.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> After thinking about this for 5 years, and seeing actual descriptions and checking my post history to realize I didn't actually respond to this.............. I agree.<br /> <br /> So, what were you referring to with that reference?</div> </div> </div> </div>Creature of the Light's miraculous power set is perfect for stuff like imposing your own stock footage and stylized reality on the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-13T08:39:25-07:00","id":1304626,"title":"","content":"What about doing Sealing magic similar to Naruto, Dragon Ball's &quot;Mafuba&quot;, etc. Anything from sealing fire in a scroll to imprisoning the Kukla under a mountain. Bonus points for sealing spirits in people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2800-astral","name":"Astral","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-13T09:14:15-07:00","id":1304634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/63616-forms-of-mag